-- V110 — Aria v2 substrate fix: repoint phantom field_codes to real columns
--
-- The V105–V109 auto-generated registrations snake_cased field_codes, but
-- ~30 legacy tables use camelCase columns (e.g. Ho_Sales_Order.billDate).
-- Result: 183 registered fields had NO matching physical column, so their
-- substrate form fields silently failed to read/write (the field_code vs
-- column mismatch class called out in earmsbackend/CLAUDE.md).
--
-- Surfaced by the substrate-parity harness P1 check
-- (com.aria.integration.parity.SubstrateParityHarness#assertSchemaFaithful).
-- This migration repoints the 165 UNAMBIGUOUS cases (exactly one case/
-- underscore-insensitive column match, target not already registered).
-- Each UPDATE is idempotent and guarded against the uq_field unique key.
--
-- NOT touched (need human adjudication, see docs / session notes):
--   * 16 truly-orphaned fields (no column matches even case-insensitively)
--   * entity 'Mode' → table m11_ai_agent_mode (table does not exist)
-- Pure substrate data change: no @Entity, no business table altered.

UPDATE entity_field_registry SET field_code='dedLorryfreight' WHERE entity_code='BillInward' AND field_code='ded_lorryfreight' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM (SELECT field_code FROM entity_field_registry WHERE entity_code='BillInward') e WHERE e.field_code='dedLorryfreight');
